** A body force on every element and a pressure on the top surface, together with an equal-value
** penalty constraint coupling the whole top edge across the subdomains. Each load is evaluated by the
** process computing its element and completed at the interface like the element forces. Runs
** distributed, bit-identical to a serial run (U.ref) on any number of processes.
*material, name=linearElastic, id=le
30000.0, 0.15, 1e-6

*modelGenerator, generator=planeRectQuad, name=gen
elType=CPE4
nX=8
nY=8
l=100
h=100

*constraint, type=equalValuePenalty, name=myConstraint
nSet=gen_top
field=displacement
component=1
penalty=1e4

*section, name=section1, thickness=1.0, material=le, type=plane
all

*job, name=nedloadsjob, domain=2d
*solver, solver=NEDMPI, name=theSolver
output-frequency=13

*fieldOutput
>>perNode, name=displacement, elSet=all, field=displacement, result=U

*step, type=adaptiveForExplicitSimulations, solver=theSolver
maxInc=1, minInc=1e-12, maxNumInc=400, maxIter=25, stepLength=1e-2
>>dirichlet, name=bottom, nSet=gen_bottom, field=displacement, 1=0.0, 2=0.0
>>bodyForce, name=gravity, elSet=all, forceVector='0.0, -0.01', f(t)=t
>>distributedload, name=pTop, surface=gen_top, magnitude=0.5, f(t)=t, type=pressure
